ukbx@rzstud1.rz.uni-karlsruhe.de (Jerome Waibel) writes:

>If I don't kill the ghost, will the bones-file be erased, or may it reapear 
>another game?

It doesn't matter if you destroyed the ghost or not, the bones file always
gets deleted when you enter the bones level (that is, when the game decides
to read the bones), and it may only be recreated if you die on the same
level.

>Can there be more than one ghost in a bones file, i.e. if I die in a bones-
>level, will there two ghosts wandering around?

Yes. I have seen bones level with 3 or 4 of my ghosts when there has been
an especially nasty moster who killed me in the first place.. like one
pit fiend wielding the Stormbringer somewhere in the Gnomish Mines..

>And what if I die in a level number that has a ghost file, but it wasn't 
>loaded in my game? Will my bones-file be appended to the existing?

No. If the game will create a new bones file, it will overwrite the 
existing one.

>Why do I sometimes know the name of my former pet (I'm playing on an amiga,
>so all bones are mine) and sometimes don't? Or are these nameless pets
>no 'ghost'-pets?

Not all dogs and cats are pets.. but I think that if the animal had a name
when the bones level was created, it will keep the name when you enter
the bones level.

>Is the stuff of the ghost-pile always cursed, without any exceptions?

Not always, not all the stuff. But often enough that you can assume any
single item of the ghost pile to be probably cursed.
There is one sure thing: if something was blessed when the ghost level
was created, it won't be cursed when you find it. And if it was cursed,
it will remain cursed. But if it was ucursed, it may or may not be
cursed when you find it..
